description:
# Task: Implement Turn Lifecycle Event Dispatch

## Objective

Dispatch turn_start and turn_end events around each provider.stream() call, allowing extensions to observe and modify turn context.

## Background

Each turn in the agent loop involves:
1. turn_start: Before calling provider.stream()
2. [Provider call and streaming]
3. turn_end: After response is fully processed

## TypeScript Reference

```typescript
// turn_start
if (runner.hasHandlers('turn_start')) {
    await runner.emit({
        type: 'turn_start',
        sessionId: session.id,
        turnIndex: context.turnIndex,
    });
}

// ... provider.stream() ...

// turn_end
if (runner.hasHandlers('turn_end')) {
    await runner.emit({
        type: 'turn_end',
        sessionId: session.id,
        turnIndex: context.turnIndex,
        message: assistantMessage,
        toolResults: toolResults,
    });
}
```

## Implementation

### In Agent Loop (src/agent.rs)

```rust
impl Agent {
    async fn run_turn(
        &mut self,
        turn_index: usize,
        event_dispatcher: Option<&EventDispatcher>,
    ) -> Result<TurnResult> {
        // Dispatch turn_start
        if let Some(dispatcher) = event_dispatcher {
            if dispatcher.has_handlers("turn_start") {
                let event = ExtensionEvent::TurnStart {
                    session_id: self.session.id().to_string(),
                    turn_index,
                };
                dispatcher.dispatch::<()>(event).await?;
            }
        }

        // Call provider
        let response = self.provider.stream(/* ... */).await?;

        // Process response...
        let assistant_message = self.process_response(response).await?;
        let tool_results = self.execute_tools(&assistant_message).await?;

        // Dispatch turn_end
        if let Some(dispatcher) = event_dispatcher {
            if dispatcher.has_handlers("turn_end") {
                let event = ExtensionEvent::TurnEnd {
                    session_id: self.session.id().to_string(),
                    turn_index,
                    message: assistant_message.clone(),
                    tool_results: tool_results.clone(),
                };
                dispatcher.dispatch::<()>(event).await?;
            }
        }

        Ok(TurnResult {
            message: assistant_message,
            tool_results,
        })
    }
}
```

## Event Data

### turn_start
```json
{
    "type": "turn_start",
    "sessionId": "abc-123",
    "turnIndex": 0
}
```

### turn_end
```json
{
    "type": "turn_end",
    "sessionId": "abc-123",
    "turnIndex": 0,
    "message": { "role": "assistant", "content": [...] },
    "toolResults": [{ "toolCallId": "...", "content": [...] }]
}
```

## Handler Examples

```javascript
// Log turn timing
let turnStart;
ctx.on('turn_start', (event) => {
    turnStart = Date.now();
    console.log(`Turn ${event.turnIndex} starting`);
});

ctx.on('turn_end', (event) => {
    const duration = Date.now() - turnStart;
    console.log(`Turn ${event.turnIndex} completed in ${duration}ms`);
    console.log(`Tool calls: ${event.toolResults.length}`);
});
```

## Testing

1. Unit test: turn_start fires before provider call
2. Unit test: turn_end fires after processing
3. Unit test: turn_index increments correctly
4. Unit test: message and toolResults included in turn_end
5. Integration test: Full turn lifecycle

## Dependencies

- Depends on: bd-tg4w (EventDispatcher)
- Part of: bd-10vp (Extension Event Hook Dispatch feature)

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] turn_start dispatched before provider call
- [ ] turn_end dispatched after processing
- [ ] Event data correct
- [ ] Handler errors don't crash agent
- [ ] Unit tests pass

# Task: Implement get_registered_tools() in PiJsRuntime

## Objective

Add a method to PiJsRuntime that queries the JS runtime for all tools registered by extensions.

## Background

Extensions register tools in JS via `pi.registerTool()`. These are stored in the JS registry object. We need to access this from Rust to build the tool list for the agent.

## Implementation

### JS Side (in PI_BRIDGE_JS)

The registry already exists:
```javascript
const __pi_registry = {
    tools: new Map(),
    commands: new Map(),
    // ...
};

pi.registerTool = function(config) {
    __pi_registry.tools.set(config.name, config);
};
```

Add a getter function:
```javascript
globalThis.__pi_get_registered_tools = function() {
    const tools = [];
    for (const [name, config] of __pi_registry.tools) {
        tools.push({
            name: config.name,
            label: config.label || config.name,
            description: config.description || "",
            parameters: config.parameters || { type: "object", properties: {} },
        });
    }
    return JSON.stringify(tools);
};
```

### Rust Side

```rust
impl PiJsRuntime {
    /// Get all tools registered by extensions.
    /// 
    /// Returns a list of tool definitions that can be wrapped
    /// and added to the agent's tool registry.
    pub async fn get_registered_tools(&self) -> Result<Vec<ExtensionToolDef>> {
        let result = self.eval("__pi_get_registered_tools()").await?;

        let tools_json = result.as_str()
            .ok_or_else(|| anyhow!("Expected string from __pi_get_registered_tools"))?;

        let tools: Vec<ExtensionToolDef> = serde_json::from_str(tools_json)?;
        Ok(tools)
    }
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Deserialize)]
pub struct ExtensionToolDef {
    pub name: String,
    pub label: String,
    pub description: String,
    pub parameters: serde_json::Value,
}
```

## Testing

1. Unit test: No tools registered → empty list
2. Unit test: One tool registered → list of 1
3. Unit test: Multiple tools → all returned
4. Unit test: Tool definition fields correct

## Dependencies

- Part of: bd-1yo9 (Extension Tool Registration)

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] __pi_get_registered_tools() added to JS bridge
- [ ] get_registered_tools() method in PiJsRuntime
- [ ] Returns correct ExtensionToolDef structs
- [ ] Unit tests pass

# Task: Implement UI Hostcall Dispatch

## Objective

Implement the UI hostcall handler that routes pi.ui.* calls from JS to the Rust UiContext.

## Background

Extensions call pi.ui methods which become UI hostcalls. The dispatch handler must:
1. Receive the hostcall from JS
2. Route to appropriate UiContext method
3. For operations returning handles, return the handle ID
4. For async operations (askUser), handle Promise resolution

## Hostcall Protocol

### Request Format
```json
{
    "type": "ui",
    "method": "showSpinner" | "updateSpinner" | "stopSpinner" | ...,
    "args": { ... }
}
```

### Methods

1. **showSpinner**: { message: string } → handle ID
2. **updateSpinner**: { id: string, message: string } → void
3. **stopSpinner**: { id: string } → void
4. **showProgress**: { total: number, message?: string } → handle ID
5. **incrementProgress**: { id: string, amount?: number } → void
6. **finishProgress**: { id: string } → void
7. **showNotification**: { message: string, type?: string } → void
8. **setStatusLine**: { text: string } → void
9. **clearStatusLine**: {} → void
10. **askUser**: { prompt: string, options?: object } → string (async)

## Implementation

### Dispatch Handler

```rust
impl HostcallDispatcher {
    async fn dispatch_ui(
        &self,
        method: &str,
        args: serde_json::Value,
    ) -> Result<HostcallResponse> {
        let ui = self.ui_context.as_ref()
            .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("No UI context bound"))?;

        match method {
            "showSpinner" => {
                let message = args.get("message")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .unwrap_or("Loading...");

                let id = ui.show_spinner(message)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!({ "id": id })))
            }

            "updateSpinner" => {
                let id = args.get("id")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'id' parameter"))?;
                let message = args.get("message")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'message' parameter"))?;

                ui.update_spinner(id, message)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(null)))
            }

            "stopSpinner" => {
                let id = args.get("id")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'id' parameter"))?;

                ui.stop_spinner(id)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(null)))
            }

            "showProgress" => {
                let total = args.get("total")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_u64())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'total' parameter"))?;
                let message = args.get("message")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str());

                let id = ui.show_progress(total, message)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!({ "id": id })))
            }

            "incrementProgress" => {
                let id = args.get("id")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'id' parameter"))?;
                let amount = args.get("amount")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_u64())
                    .unwrap_or(1);

                ui.increment_progress(id, amount)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(null)))
            }

            "finishProgress" => {
                let id = args.get("id")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'id' parameter"))?;

                ui.finish_progress(id)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(null)))
            }

            "showNotification" => {
                let message = args.get("message")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'message' parameter"))?;
                let notification_type = match args.get("type").and_then(|v| v.as_str()) {
                    Some("warn") | Some("warning") => NotificationType::Warning,
                    Some("error") => NotificationType::Error,
                    _ => NotificationType::Info,
                };

                ui.show_notification(message, notification_type)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(null)))
            }

            "setStatusLine" => {
                let text = args.get("text")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'text' parameter"))?;

                ui.set_status_line(text)?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(null)))
            }

            "clearStatusLine" => {
                ui.clear_status_line()?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(null)))
            }

            "askUser" => {
                let prompt = args.get("prompt")
                    .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                    .ok_or_else(|| anyhow\!("Missing 'prompt' parameter"))?;

                let options = if let Some(opts) = args.get("options") {
                    serde_json::from_value(opts.clone())?
                } else {
                    AskOptions::default()
                };

                // This is async - will resolve the promise
                let result = ui.ask_user(prompt, options).await?;
                Ok(HostcallResponse::success(json\!(result)))
            }

            _ => Err(anyhow\!("Unknown UI method: {}", method)),
        }
    }
}
```

### JS Bridge (pi.ui)

Update PI_BRIDGE_JS to expose UI methods:

```javascript
pi.ui = {
    showSpinner(message) {
        const result = __pi_hostcall_sync({ type: 'ui', method: 'showSpinner', args: { message } });
        const handle = { id: result.id };
        handle.update = (msg) => __pi_hostcall_sync({ 
            type: 'ui', method: 'updateSpinner', args: { id: handle.id, message: msg } 
        });
        handle.stop = () => __pi_hostcall_sync({ 
            type: 'ui', method: 'stopSpinner', args: { id: handle.id } 
        });
        return handle;
    },

    showProgress(total, message) {
        const result = __pi_hostcall_sync({ type: 'ui', method: 'showProgress', args: { total, message } });
        const handle = { id: result.id };
        handle.increment = (amount = 1) => __pi_hostcall_sync({ 
            type: 'ui', method: 'incrementProgress', args: { id: handle.id, amount } 
        });
        handle.finish = () => __pi_hostcall_sync({ 
            type: 'ui', method: 'finishProgress', args: { id: handle.id } 
        });
        return handle;
    },

    showNotification(message, type = 'info') {
        __pi_hostcall_sync({ type: 'ui', method: 'showNotification', args: { message, type } });
    },

    setStatusLine(text) {
        __pi_hostcall_sync({ type: 'ui', method: 'setStatusLine', args: { text } });
    },

    clearStatusLine() {
        __pi_hostcall_sync({ type: 'ui', method: 'clearStatusLine', args: {} });
    },

    async askUser(prompt, options) {
        return await __pi_hostcall({ type: 'ui', method: 'askUser', args: { prompt, options } });
    },
};
```

